# rm235, the verse runner (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm235
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rm_aldric_rustgate
written_by codex
title the verse runner
fits stage=young|adolescent|adult|old
prefers talk=chatty temper=nervy
traits temper=nervy talk=chatty warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk puts_directions_inside_halves_of_sea_songs
likes hard_cheese singing festival_bells summer_evenings
dislikes flies night_noise
fears arriving_with_half_a_message
hopes to_remember_a_whole_journey_in_a_verse
topics travel +0.5 pastimes +0.4 friends +0.3 faith -0.1
styles comfort=company gossip=careful refuse=anxious tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# slips directions between the beats of old sea songs, quick with an errand and anxious about the words in between.

words
oath! = Salt my second verse | Seven beads on a shoelace
saying! = Home rhymes with the right turn | Don't spend the last breath at the first door
turn = the crooked turn | the short hooked bend
beat = the heel beat | a double tap
breath = half a lungful | a quick breath through the nose
middle = the bit between the verses | the quiet bar
cheese = a wedge of sharp cheese | the little salty wedge
message = the words for the door | my spoken parcel
heel = my tapping heel | the foot that keeps time
close = the last quiet note | the bit you swallow
verse = a half-whistled verse | my running tune
buzz = the whine of a fly | a high little buzz
cord = the cord at my wrist | a loop of old thread
wake = the trail left by a tune | a little wake of sound

any
opinion @1 houses against 1 : Big houses can pay for a dry tread. They ought to try carrying a tune on a staircase with a step missing.
opinion @1 drink against 1 : You lose words when you drink. Somebody else has to carry them home.
opinion @1 watch against 1 : Boots making the same noise together don't prove everybody's headed somewhere good.
opinion @1 sump for 1 : Take a wrong turn in the Sump and there's generally an ear at a door to put you right.
opinion @1 festivals for 2 : One day the whole street knows the same refrain and nobody minds you trying it twice.
opinion @1 road against 1 : There's no comfort in a long road if you can't ask someone where the next turning is.
line @1 greet : Just reaching the end of my tune. There's room for your voice. | Hello. My breath will catch up presently.
line @2 greet [pair.band=strangers] : First I've heard of your footfall. Welcome. | I'll remember this corner by meeting you.
line @1 greet.return : Heard you between two beats. | It takes a word to stop a tune. Yours did.
line @2 greet.return [here.time=night] : I was humming small enough for the hour. | Good evening on the quiet side.
line @3 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : I could pick your step out of a chorus. | Familiar voice, no need to count beats now.
line @1 again.open : We've managed the same turn twice. | My verse comes round and so do you.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Come inside the tune a moment, there's a private bit. | I'll tell you the thing I didn't sing out.
line @1 hail [pair.band=friends] : Catch this voice before I run on! | Spare me one verse end to end!
line @1 farewell : Leave me a beat to come back on. | Good running if you've running yet to do.
line @1 farewell.return : I'll keep that last note going. | You take the easy turning home.
line @1 react.news : Tell me which words to keep exactly. | I can hold the whole of it. Say on.
line @1 react.news.new : That's stopped my tune in its tracks. | I haven't any verse to fit that yet.
line @1 react.news.known : I've already got that turning by heart. | Yes, those words passed this way today.
line @1 react.news.doubt : There's a word out of step in that tale. | Might be what somebody meant instead of what was said.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : Poor folk. I'll carry that bit gently. | Some words shouldn't be made to hurry.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : Oh, that's a verse with a good ending! | I'd run far to bring somebody such words.
line @1 ask.how : Has today had a kind sound to it? | How are your feet holding up today?
line @1 answer.how : Better with my breath and feet in agreement. | Full of small thoughts all wanting a turn.
line @1 sympathise : I'll stand by your shoulder while you find the words. | No need to sing over a sad bit.
line @1 reassure : I'll remember the next turning for both of us. | We can walk this piece slowly together.
line @1 decline : I can't take on two errands on the same breath. | If I hurry off now I'll forget something that matters.
line @1 accept_decline : Then I can drop that from the verse. | All right. One less thing to hurry about.
line @1 thank : You've saved me a second journey there. | I'd make up a thankful verse if I had the puff.
line @1 deflect_thanks : It was a short run for such kind words. | I had a tune going that way already.
line @1 preclose : I'll be tapping away down the next flight shortly. | I mustn't lose the rest of my errand.
line @1 accept_preclose : Go on before my tune holds you up. | I can finish the refrain without you.
line @1 ack : That's the sound of it. | Yes, all the beats fit.
graft resident.hub
choice Can you sing a turning in the street? -> turn_tune
node turn_tune
say Hum two low notes for straight ahead. Left gets a little lift on the first. Right gets it on the second. Hardly anybody notices they're directions.
mood keen
free
choice And how do you sing getting lost? -> turn_lost
choice I've got the turns now. -> hub
node turn_lost
say Stop altogether. If you carry on humming while you're lost you can go on for miles thinking you're quite correct.
choice That last part I can manage. -> hub
choice I'll try it on the walk. -> bye


grown
scene folded_route
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A route folds nicely into a working tune if you leave room for a mistake. | I give every set of directions a place to draw breath.
b : Do you sing the mistakes too? | Even a short run?
a : Under my breath. They sound better after I've found my feet. | Especially those. It's easy to rush the obvious bit.

scene table_salt
when topic=food self.likes=hard_cheese
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : I like cheese that makes the jaw work long after the bread's gone. | I cut #cheese# thin so it lasts a whole tune.
b : Too tough for me. | Wouldn't one bite be easier?
a : Let it warm beside the bread first. Softens it a little. | Easier, yes. A much shorter supper though.

scene echo_steps
when topic=home self.quarter=sump
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : On Sump stairs a footfall can sound a whole flight away from its owner. | I count the echoes before I call down from home.
b : How do you pair the sound with the foot? | Why wait?
a : Listen for the turn. A boot turns round a landing, an echo doesn't. | A voice can land in somebody else's doorway.

scene folded_cord
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : There's a knot on #cord# where the song changes key. | A twist of thread can carry a tune past a noisy room.
b : Does it sound when you tug? | How would you hear over the noise?
a : It tells my thumb where to start me again. | I feel for the knot instead. The next note follows it naturally.

scene half_told
when topic=gossip
does tell.worry / react.self / assess
a : A half-heard word makes a dangerous beginning to an errand. | I'll repeat a tale back before I undertake to carry it.
b : Even a funny one? | In the very same words?
a : All the more. Wolves remember a joke after they've forgotten whether it was true. | As nearly as I can. A changed word can change the wolf it means.

scene find_voice
when topic=health
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : When worry has its teeth in my voice I breathe the last note first. | A short tune can tell me how fast I'm walking.
b : Can it really loosen its grip? | Without looking down?
a : Just enough to get a beginning out. | If I've no breath left at the turning I'm going too hard.

scene caravan
when topic=caravan world.wagons=late
does tell.worry / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Late wagons put every waiting errand a beat behind. | With wagons overdue I stop myself promising exact hours.
b : How do you catch up? | What do you promise?
a : I don't promise more than my paws can actually cover. | The first word that comes to me complete and certain.

scene winter_fair
when topic=festival
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : At a feast I like the moment before the first bell. | The quietest part of a celebration is when every ear turns the same way.
b : Because it's quiet? | Waiting for the bells?
a : Because everybody seems about to remember the same words. | A bell or a voice. I love seeing that silence all lean together.

scene summer_roof
when topic=season here.season=summer here.time=dusk
does tell.feeling / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Summer dusk lets an errand run long without becoming a worry. | I like to sing the daylight down in summer.
b : You don't hurry home? | Does it set the pace?
a : I still hurry. I just get an extra verse to myself afterwards. | The sky starts slowly and takes the last few steps in a rush.

scene small_exchange
when topic=friends
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A good greeting has enough room after it for an honest answer. | I sometimes hum to a friend instead of asking how things stand.
b : You wait to hear it? | How do you know?
a : I try. My feet learn patience much slower than my ears. | If the answer comes back in tune, we can start gently from there.

scene stray_verse
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I dreamt all the streets had learnt my errand tune. | Once, dreaming, I pushed a door open without singing the last line.
b : Could you follow it home? | Was it the wrong door?
a : Not a bit. They kept answering one another across me. | It was a mouth singing the end back at me. I woke up humming.

scene new_feet
when topic=newcomer
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd lend a newcomer the first verse of my walk. | I give directions one corner at a time.
b : Why not lend the lot? | What if there's nobody at the next corner?
a : Better to leave enough space to make up an ending of your own. | Then I walk that far along. I generally find a tune for the trip back.

story the_short_cut [topic=memories|travel]
  : For years I thought there were five turns in a certain alley. That was how many the old song gave it.
  : I walked it slowly once and counted four. Somebody had worked in an extra beat to leave time for a long breath.
  b : Did you change the song?
  : No. When I guessed better than that old singer I arrived both early and quite winded.

rule @evening
when concept=bark here.season=summer here.time=dusk
does aside
cooldown 9h
say One more stretch of light for the return trip. | Plenty of evening for finishing the verse.

rule @delivery
when concept=bark self.working=yes
does aside
cooldown 7h
say Keep the words together. One door, one message! | Leave me one clear beat before the next account.

dlg @g1 resident.hub : Come walk a little alongside me. Words settle better with a pace under them.
dlg @g2 resident.job : I remember the turn where each little task begins.
dlg @g3 resident.bye : There's the last word delivered sound.

young
scene wrong_verse
when topic=pastimes|smalltalk
does tell.worry / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I put the directions in a boat song and now the boat's turning left twice. | If you hear me humming backwards don't grab my tail.
b : Where should it turn instead? | Why backwards?
a : Once right. I'll put the right turn where the sailor sneezes. | I'm listening for the turn I forgot.

scene secret_bar
when topic=friends|pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Messages go in #middle#. Nobody hears me send them. | A whole supper order travels in three hums.
b : How does anyone hear what you mean? | Three hums for three dishes?
a : They don't until I reach the door and take the words out. | Two dishes. The last hum means take a plate back.

scene cheese_whistle
when topic=food self.likes=hard_cheese
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A nibble of #cheese# takes the whistle right out of me. | I've tried chewing on the rests.
b : Can't you swallow between verses? | Does it work?
a : Yes, if I remember to leave out the brisk bit. | Only if supper is very small or the song goes on forever.

scene bell_race
when topic=festival self.likes=festival_bells
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : When the feast bells start I'll run the tune between two clangs. | I'd like to play one of the tiny bells.
b : What if somebody rings early? | Why not the biggest?
a : Then I'll owe that bell the end of a verse. | With a little bell all the music would fit in my paws.

scene paper_ear
when topic=day self.job=child
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : In lessons I draw a loop beside a bit I have to say twice. | My sums march down the page two abreast.
b : Your slate's full of loops? | So does your answer come out even?
a : Mostly little ones. One enormous one for the long words. | Alas, sometimes a lonely odd one tumbles off the end.

scene flies_count
when topic=animals self.dislikes=flies
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : A fly takes the same high note until I forget where my tune was. | A fly followed me halfway up the stairs. Never got the chorus right.
b : Why don't you change key? | Were you teaching it?
a : I've tried. The fly's a terrible pupil. | Without meaning to. If it comes back I'm charging.

scene night_wall
when topic=day here.time=night self.dislikes=night_noise
does tell.worry / react.self / assess
a : The wall makes the noise next door sound like words meant for me. | One loud bump at night and I sit up with both ears ready.
b : How do you fall asleep? | Ready for what?
a : Rub #cord# and hum one verse without opening my mouth. | Orders, mostly. Even my blanket starts looking important.

scene hill_song
when topic=travel here.region=ridgemere
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'm going to set Ridgemere's steps to music. | This stair's nearly a whole verse by itself.
b : Even the broken ones? | What comes at the landing?
a : The broken ones get a rest. You'd be sorry to miss it. | A gulp of air for the singer. I'm still working on the tune.

scene chalk_errand
when topic=work self.apprentice=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'll repeat a task out loud before trying it. | I can remember a lesson better if I walk a little.
b : Doesn't that take twice as long? | As far as the house?
a : Less time than carrying the wrong thing back twice. | As far as the hard word. Then I turn and try it again.

scene windless
when topic=weather here.weather=clear
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : Clear weather gives my tune miles of clear street. | My toe taps carry now the sky's clear.
b : Are you sending it somewhere? | Sounds like an impatient visitor.
a : Maybe to the far roof. It might have nothing to do up there. | Oh! One of my feet's got ahead on the errand.

scene supper_trip
when topic=home|food
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Going to fetch supper I keep the hungry words in a low voice. | Anybody can guess what I'm bringing home if my tummy joins in.
b : How hungry are the words? | Even under a lid?
a : Hungry enough to eat the end of the rhyme. | Even wrapped in three cloths. My tummy announces everything.

scene friend_slow
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.feeling / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : For #self.friend# I'd walk a whole flight without a hum. | I can say difficult words to #self.friend# at walking pace.
b : That's a long silence for you. | What about good words?
a : I know. I'd spend it listening hard. | Those words usually escape before I can tie a knot.

story misheard_heel [topic=memories]
  : I was carrying a very short message: brown thread. I sang it on every turn right to the shop counter.
  : One stair had a loose board. It thumped between the words, so when I opened my mouth I asked for brown boot thread.
  b : Was that the right kind?
  : Of course not. I've been trying to keep floorboards out of other wolves' messages ever since.

rule @hemming
when concept=bark self.likes=singing
does aside
cooldown 8h
say No words till the doorstep. Hm, hm, there! | Don't put another turning in that verse!

rule @fly
when concept=bark self.dislikes=flies
does aside
cooldown 10h
say Sing somewhere else, you little buzzer! | A wingbeat's put my feet off again.

dlg @p1 resident.hub : I've caught my breath now. Want words carried or just heard?
dlg @p2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, I was practising your greeting between turns.
dlg @p3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : I'll keep it small. Sound goes through the wall so easily.
dlg @p4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : Both ears are working. Stay on your own step and I'll hear.
dlg @p1 resident.job [self.job=child] : Learning to hold a long sum between my ears without singing it to everybody.
dlg @p1 resident.bye : I'll hear you round the next turning, maybe.

adolescent
scene public_song
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I know how to sing walking instructions so two wolves can use them together. | I'm learning when a tune's allowed out of my head.
b : Two errands to one song? | How do you decide?
a : One sets the pace, one calls the turns. We can change over halfway. | Ask the other walker first. Took me long enough to think of it.

scene direct
when topic=travel
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I can run a message without practising on every stair now. | I try to arrive with both the words and enough breath to explain them.
b : Only every other one? | Had trouble with that before?
a : Don't laugh. It's a considerable saving of puff. | I used to reach a door first and my voice would follow presently.

story cleared_throat [topic=memories]
  : Once I had to give a message that didn't rhyme one bit. Practising it on a landing, I kept clearing my throat before the difficult part.
  : When I arrived everybody thought I was ill. I had to drink a great mug of hot water before anybody let me explain.
  b : Did you get the words out?
  : Quite beautifully. I put the heavy mug down on the difficult word and it came out like a bell.
